{title: I'll Play You Home}
by Colin Alvarez
Heavy 12/8

{start_of_bridge: Intro}
[Fmaj7]  [Am]
Vamp before verse comes in
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]
Pop, you never played, but you knew every song
[Fmaj7] 
Raised me on that old familiar sound
[Dsus2]
you’d crank up Stevie, Jimi, and page
         [Am]                   [E]
Sayin’ “Son, that’s a new family found’
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]
We lost mom, and with her so much more
[Fmaj7]
Secrets can’t stay buried too long
[Dsus2]
You ran out west, chasing your setting sun,
         [Am]                    [ E]
But old shadows knew right from wrong
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
    [Am]                        [Fmaj7]
But pop i see you nod when I hit that bend
       [Dsus2]                [E]
Still see you in the ones you lost
 [Am]                                 [E]
We’ve had our silence, we’ve had our sin
[Dsus 2]                              [Am]   [E7]
But I saw your pain and  the cost
 [Am]                  [Fmaj7]
Cant imagine, what you faced alone
[Dsus2]                       [Am]  [E]
Id give anything, for one more day
[C]                  [D]                [Fmaj7]
Goodbyes too hard, the silence too deep,
[E]
So I will play you home.

[Fmaj7] 2 bars      [Am] 2 Bars
{comment: Vamp on this until next verse}
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]                        
You weren’t perfect, and neither am I
[Fmaj7]
A reflection of the man I saw
[Dsus2]
Times too cold, and the distance so far
[Am]                            [E]
But in the music I still hear you call
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Am]
In whatever comes after, if there is a stage
[Fmaj7]
Free from all the burden and pain
[Dsus2]
Know your boy still sings your song
              [Am]                   [E]
and looks for peace in whatever remains
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_chorus}
[Am]                            [Fmaj7]
But pop can you see me when I hit that bend?
[Dsus2]                 [E]
Do you see me in the ones you lost
[Am]                      [Fmaj7]
We had our silence, we hid our sins
[Dsus2]             [Am]  [E]
But I felt your pain   and its cost

[Am]                    [Fmaj7]
could you see what we faced alone?
             [Dsus2]                 [Am]
What would you do with one more day
[C]                   [Dsus2]       [Fmaj7]
Goodbyes too hard, the silence too deep,
[E] [*(ring)]
So I will play you home.



